Read up on the info page for GNU gettext. If format strings are being 
used properly, then you may be able to use some funky format specifiers 
to rearrange things. In any case, putting translations directly into 
the code base is a *very bad idea* since the DevTeam can't possibly 
accept them, and merging version updates would be extremely difficult 
otherwise (replacing every string in the program is an *exceptionally 
bad idea*.) Also an issue are strings in tables and in the data files. 
Because of that, SGT (Static GetText - http://www.jimrandomh.org/sgt - 
basically, it does gettext-style replacements at compile time, but it 
is *extremely immature*) might be a better tool to use than GNU 
gettext. (Or it might be awful. I wrote it for a calculator roguelike 
myself.)

Also, beware the wishing code. It's a giant ball of mud which will 
probably need a complete rewrite for each language supported.

